      "nets": ["NET0003", "NET0010"],
      "observed": "J6 AVR-ISP-6 pin 4 (MOSI) is connected to NET0003, which runs to U3 pin 3 and U4 pin 3 (PB4/XTAL2). The ATtiny PB0/MOSI pins, U3 pin 5 and U4 pin 5, are on NET0010 and are not connected to J6 pin 4.",
      "expected": "J6 pin 4 (MOSI) should connect to NET0010 at U3 pin 5 and U4 pin 5 (PB0/MOSI), matching the standard AVR ISP pinout for the ATtiny45/ATtiny13.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "Sheet 1, J6 area: 'MOSI' pin 4 is labeled NET0003; U3/U4 PB0 pin 5 is labeled NET0010."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "AVR ISP programming through J6 cannot drive the ATtiny MOSI pin, so programming will fail. The programmer's MOSI signal will instead drive the PB4/fan-control node, potentially disturbing fan control.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The board contains a clear ISP miswiring: J6 MOSI is tied to NET0003/PB4 instead of NET0010/PB0, so ISP programming will not work and the wrong MCU node may be driven."
}

